# Fibonacci anyons and their fusion ring, the simplest particles that compute. There is one nontrivial type, tau, with
# the fusion rule that two taus fuse either to the vacuum or back to a tau, tau times tau is one plus tau. The fusion
# outcomes are recorded by the multiplicity, the number of times a given anyon appears in the product of two others, and
# these multiplicities are the structure constants of the fusion ring. This file DEFINES the Fibonacci multiplicities as a
# function on the two anyon labels and PROVES the two laws that make them a commutative fusion ring: the vacuum is a unit,
# fusing any anyon with the vacuum returns that same anyon, and fusion is commutative, the multiplicity is unchanged when
# the two factors are swapped. These are the ring axioms that let the anyons carry and combine quantum information, proved
# over the actual anyon type. The dimension of the space of ways to fuse a line of taus grows by the Fibonacci recurrence,
# which is why the quantum dimension of a tau is the golden ratio, tying this fusion ring to the golden growth of the
# substrate.

# The two anyon labels: the vacuum and the nontrivial tau.
form anyon
  case vacuum
  case tau

# The Kronecker delta on anyons, one when the two labels agree and zero otherwise, the multiplicity of fusing with the
# vacuum.
task same-anyon
  take b, like anyon
  take c, like anyon
  like natural-number
  fork case, read b
    case vacuum
      fork case, read c
        case vacuum
          send back
            code 1
        case tau
          send back
            code 0
    case tau
      fork case, read c
        case vacuum
          send back
            code 0
        case tau
          send back
            code 1

# The Fibonacci fusion multiplicity: how many times c appears in a times b. Vacuum is a unit, and tau times tau is one
# plus tau, so every multiplicity is one except vacuum-times-vacuum-gives-tau and the two vacuum-tau clashes, which are
# zero.
task combine
  take a, like anyon
  take b, like anyon
  take c, like anyon
  like natural-number
  fork case, read a
    case vacuum
      send back
        call same-anyon
          read b
          read c
    case tau
      fork case, read b
        case vacuum
          send back
            call same-anyon
              make tau
              read c
        case tau
          send back
            code 1

# THE VACUUM IS A UNIT: fusing the vacuum with any anyon b returns exactly b, so the multiplicity of c in vacuum times b
# is one precisely when c equals b, combine(vacuum, b, c) = same-anyon(b, c), for all b and c. Proved by induction over the
# anyon labels.
rule vacuum-is-the-fusion-unit
  seat b, like anyon
  seat c, like anyon
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call combine
        make vacuum
        read b
        read c
      call same-anyon
        read b
        read c
  fold b, c

# FUSION IS COMMUTATIVE: the multiplicity is unchanged when the two fused anyons are swapped, combine(a, b, c) = combine(b, a,
# c), for all a, b and c, so the fusion ring is commutative. Proved by simultaneous induction over the three anyon labels.
rule fusion-is-commutative
  seat a, like anyon
  seat b, like anyon
  seat c, like anyon
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call combine
        read a
        read b
        read c
      call combine
        read b
        read a
        read c
  fold a, b, c
